Synchronous buck converter power stage, IHP SG13G2 high-voltage MOS
* 3.3 V at a duty cycle of 0.35 and 10 MHz into 12 Ohm, 0.96 V at the output. A PMOS of
* 2 mm and an NMOS of 1 mm in fingers of 10 um, driven with dead times of 3 ns and 2 ns,
* 1 uH with 50 mOhm and 10 nF, 50 pF at the switching node. Start from zero output,
* 300 switching periods.
.lib "ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib" mos_tt
vin vin 0 dc 3.3
vgp gp 0 dc 3.3 pulse(3.3 0 2n 1n 1n 34n 100n)
vgn gn 0 dc 0 pulse(0 3.3 40n 1n 1n 57n 100n)
xmp sw gp vin vin sg13_hv_pmos w=2000u l=0.45u ng=200
xmn sw gn 0 0 sg13_hv_nmos w=1000u l=0.45u ng=100
csw sw 0 50p
l1 sw lx 1u
rl lx out 50m
c1 out 0 10n
rload out 0 12
.save v(gp) v(gn) v(sw) v(out)
.op
.tran 1n 30u
.end
